s://waymo.com/blog/2026/09/transit-rewards/"},{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"Flimm"},"title":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"Obscura: VPN that can't log your activity"},"url":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"https://obscura.com/#faq-technical"}},"_tags":["story","author_Flimm","story_49807003","front_page"],"author":"Flimm","children":[49807254,49807268,49807289,49807302,49807312,49807322,49807404,49807421,49807445,49807458,49807483,49807667,49807802,49807822,49807857,49807934,49807977,49808595,49808633,49809060,49809358,49810114,49810353,49810690,49811011,49811098,49811200,49811530,49811611,49812697,49812829,49812850,49813408,49814168],"created_at":"2026-09-22T19:40:28Z","created_at_i":1790106028,"num_comments":117,"objectID":"49807003","points":152,"story_id":49807003,"title":"Obscura: VPN that can't log your activity","updated_at":"2026-09-23T12:09:05Z","url":"https://obscura.com/#faq-technical"},{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"florianstandhar"},"story_text":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"Hi HN! I built JevBench because Jev kicks ass, and the world deserves to know how the serious open source and fake lookalike projects <i>really</i> perform in comparison.<p>Jev-class models return bounded choices and probabilities instead of text, and are disruptively faster and cheaper than LLMs, while being similarly intelligent on the text input they operate on.<p>JevBench allows looking at accuracy, latency and price all at once, in a weighted way - you can even configure the weighting.<p>A full run asks 534 English decisions. The v1.3 score combines chance-corrected Intelligence, Calibration, Speed and Cost.<p>Leaderboard right now:<p><pre><code>  #1 - Jev            74.4\n  #2 - SemIf          73.1\n  #3 - djev           73.0\n  #4 - Winnow-12B Q8  71.2\n  #5 reflex 4B        70.3.\n</code></pre>\nMIT harness, public items, frozen artifacts, scoring code and public per-task outcomes:<p><a href=\"https://github.com/fstandhartinger/jevbench\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://github.com/fstandhartinger/jevbench</a><p>Two no-signup demos:<p><a href=\"https://who-is-right.app.mintapis.com\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://who-is-right.app.mintapis.com</a><p><a href=\"https://is-it-ai-slop.app.mintapis.com\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://is-it-ai-slop.app.mintapis.com</a><p>Limitations: English-only; latency from one German server; local/demo latency gets a disclosed \u00d72 adjustment (+150 ms on my servers) which is an informed assumption; held-out prompts still reach evaluated services; ~1-point gaps can be noise.<p>Wdyt?"},"title":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"Show HN: JevBench, a reproducible benchmark for typed decision models"},"url":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"https://benchmarkheaven.com/jev-models"}},"_tags":["story","author_florianstandhar","story_49800574","show_hn","front_page"],"author":"florianstandhar","children":[49800575,49807791,49808495,49808592,49809071,49809676,49809896,49810168,49810509,49810808,49811050,49811269,49811399,49812306,49812398,49812631,49813649],"created_at":"2026-09-22T13:01:03Z","created_at_i":1790082063,"num_comments":32,"objectID":"49800574","points":114,"story_id":49800574,"story_text":"Hi HN! I built JevBench because Jev kicks ass, and the world deserves to know how the serious open source and fake lookalike projects <i>really</i> perform in comparison.<p>Jev-class models return bounded choices and probabilities instead of text, and are disruptively faster and cheaper than LLMs, while being similarly intelligent on the text input they operate on.<p>JevBench allows looking at accuracy, latency and price all at once, in a weighted way - you can even configure the weighting.<p>A full run asks 534 English decisions. The v1.3 score combines chance-corrected Intelligence, Calibration, Speed and Cost.<p>Leaderboard right now:<p><pre><code>  #1 - Jev            74.4\n  #2 - SemIf          73.1\n  #3 - djev           73.0\n  #4 - Winnow-12B Q8  71.2\n  #5 reflex 4B        70.3.\n</code></pre>\nMIT harness, public items, frozen artifacts, scoring code and public per-task outcomes:<p><a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;github.com&#x2F;fstandhartinger&#x2F;jevbench\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;github.com&#x2F;fstandhartinger&#x2F;jevbench</a><p>Two no-signup demos:<p><a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;who-is-right.app.mintapis.com\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;who-is-right.app.mintapis.com</a><p><a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;is-it-ai-slop.app.mintapis.com\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;is-it-ai-slop.app.mintapis.com</a><p>Limitations: English-only; latency from one German server; local&#x2F;demo latency gets a disclosed \u00d72 adjustment (+150 ms on my servers) which is an informed assumption; held-out prompts still reach evaluated services; ~1-point gaps can be noise.<p>Wdyt?","title":"Show HN: JevBench, a reproducible benchmark for typed decision models","updated_at":"2026-09-23T12:08:34Z","url":"https://benchmarkheaven.com/jev-models"}],"hitsPerPage":20,"nbHits":30,"nbPages":2,"page":0,"params":"tags=front_page&advancedSyntax=true&analyticsTags=backend","processingTimeMS":1,"processingTimingsMS":{"_request":{"roundTrip":20},"total":0},"query":"","serverTimeMS":1}
